**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The PTB OCDB adapter is a second `MaterialSourceProxy` over an offline snapshot of PTB's repository, kept and updated by the body the refractiveindex.info adapter already runs (001 §D '2. PTB OCDB (CC BY 4.0)'; the S13.1 mapper's note: PTB and Henke are further `MaterialSourceProxy` creates; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy': the shared body moves, it is not copied). Verified 2026-11-04: `github.com/PTB-SR/ocdb`, default branch `master`, the records at `ocdb/db/data/<name>.txt` (`Co.txt`, `Ru.txt`, `Ru_2019.txt`, `TiN.txt` …, no index file) and `ocdb/db/COPYING`, which says the data files in `data` are licensed under CC BY 4.0. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialSourceStore.fs` (step 447): (1) The snapshot body MOVES out of `createRefractiveIndexInfo` into private shapes that it and every later adapter call, its behaviour and S13.1's eight facts unchanged: `SourceSnapshotLayout = { source : MaterialSourceName; folder : FolderName }`, the snapshot folder whose siblings `<folder>.zip.tmp`, `<folder>.tmp` and `<folder>.old` an update uses; `SourceArchiveEntryChoice` = `KeepArchiveEntry` | `DropArchiveEntry`; `SourceArchiveSpec = { url : SourceArchiveUrl; requiredFile : KitRelativePath; keep : KitRelativePath -> SourceArchiveEntryChoice }`, paths relative to the archive's one top folder. On the layout: `member this.snapshotVersion` (step 447's stamp read), `member this.heldVersion : Result<MaterialSourceVersion, MaterialSourceError>` (`SourceSnapshotMissingErr` without a stamp), `member this.installFrom (staged : FolderName) (clock : ClockProvider) (files : SourceSnapshotFileCount)` (the stamp written into the staged folder, the held folder moved to `.old`, the staged one moved in, the leftovers deleted, an error moving `.old` back) and `member this.updateFromArchive (spec : SourceArchiveSpec) (downloader : SourceArchiveDownloader) (clock : ClockProvider) (observer : SourceSnapshotObserver)` (step 447's download, `listZipEntries`, top-folder check, `extractKitZip` and cancellation, keeping the file entries `spec.keep` keeps and requiring `spec.requiredFile`, else `SourceArchiveInvalidErr`). `createRefractiveIndexInfo` builds its layout and spec (`database/catalog-nk.yml` required; that file and everything under `database/data/` kept) and calls them. Each private declaration whose signature carries a bare primitive for this IO keeps step 447's `ElevationBoundary` mark. (2) `type MaterialSourceProxy with static member createPtbOcdb (sources : FolderName) (downloader : SourceArchiveDownloader) (clock : ClockProvider) : MaterialSourceProxy`, unique on its receiver (ELEV019). Building it touches nothing. `sourceName` is `MaterialSourceName "PTB OCDB"`, the folder `<sources>/ptb-ocdb`, the licence `EntryLicence "CC-BY-4.0"` and the archive `SourceArchiveUrl "https://github.com/PTB-SR/ocdb/archive/refs/heads/master.zip"`, each written there alone; its spec requires `ocdb/db/COPYING` and keeps that file and every file directly in `ocdb/db/data/` whose name ends in `.txt` (ordinal, ignoring case). `snapshotVersion` and `updateSnapshot` are the layout's. `searchRecords query`: `heldVersion`, then `query.filter` (step 443) of one hit per `.txt` file of the snapshot's `ocdb/db/data/`, in ordinal order of file name: `record = MaterialSourceRecordId <the file name>` and `name = EntryName "<its stem> (PTB OCDB)"`; an IO exception is `SourceSnapshotIoErr`. `fetchRecord record`: `heldVersion`; a record the search does not list (a separator in it included) is `SourceRecordMissingErr` naming it; otherwise the file's bytes give `recordHash = ContentHash.ofBytes <the bytes>` (step 123) and their UTF-8 text, a leading byte-order mark dropped, is `PtbOcdbText` (step 454), whose `importMaterial` error is `SourceRecordUnreadableErr` naming the record with the error's `describe`. The answer is `{ pull = { source; record; recordHash; sourceVersion = <the stamp's>; licence; citation }; material = { <the import> with name = <the hit's name> } }`, the citation `EntryCitation "PTB Optical Constants Database (OCDB), ocdb/db/data/<record>"` followed, when `headlineOpt` answers one, by `: ` and its text, so S3.3's CC-BY rule shows it (step 113). No retry, cache, mirror, second URL or setting is added (.spec-md §8). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialSources.fs`: the `MaterialSourceProxy` doc (step 443) names `createPtbOcdb` beside the other creates in no more words. Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialSourceFixture.fs` (step 447), each with a one-line doc: `ptbRecord ()` is the text of `fixtures/ptb-Co.txt`; `changedPtbRecord ()` is it with `0.96804` replaced by `0.96810`; `writePtbSnapshot (snapshot : string) (record : string) : unit` writes `ocdb/db/COPYING` (a test-local licence line), `record` as `ocdb/db/data/Co.txt`, a three-column record (step 454's header lines without the bound columns or the 3-sigma line, and two rows) as `ocdb/db/data/Ru_2019.txt` and the stamp of `2026-11-01`; `writePtbArchive (zip : string) (record : string) : unit` writes a GitHub-style archive whose one top folder `ocdb-master/` holds `README.rst`, `ocdb/db/literature.bib`, `ocdb/db/metadata/elements/Co.yaml` and the three files `writePtbSnapshot` writes but the stamp. In `MaterialSourceStoreTests`, each over a fresh sources folder: `a PTB OCDB source without a snapshot answers no version and refuses search and fetch`: `snapshotVersion` is `Ok None`, and `searchRecords` and `fetchRecord` are `SourceSnapshotMissingErr`. `a PTB OCDB snapshot lists its data records, and a fetched record is the reader's material with CC BY 4.0 and its citation`: over `writePtbSnapshot` of `ptbRecord ()`, a blank query lists `Co.txt` named `Co (PTB OCDB)` then `Ru_2019.txt`, and `co` lists `Co.txt` alone; the fetched `Co.txt` holds the physics of `(PtbOcdbText (ptbRecord ())).importMaterial`, uncertainties included, under its hit's name, the file's hash, `2026-11-01`, `CC-BY-4.0` and the citation `PTB Optical Constants Database (OCDB), ocdb/db/data/Co.txt: Optical constants for Co created by PTB`; `Ru_2019.txt` holds no uncertainty; and `../Co.txt` and `Ta.txt` answer `SourceRecordMissingErr`. `a PTB OCDB update keeps the data records and the licence file of the repository archive`: `updateSnapshot` with `copyingDownloader` of `writePtbArchive` of `changedPtbRecord ()` and `fixedClock` of 2026-11-04 answers `SourceSnapshotUpdated` of `2026-11-04` and three files, its progress reading 1 to 3 of 3; the one URL asked is the archive's; the snapshot holds exactly `.snapshot-json`, `ocdb/db/COPYING` and the two records, with no `README.rst`, `literature.bib` or metadata; and the sources folder holds nothing else. `a PTB OCDB archive without its licence file is refused and the held snapshot kept`: an archive without `ocdb/db/COPYING` answers `SourceArchiveInvalidErr`, and the held snapshot keeps its files byte for byte. `an update downloads the archive and replaces the snapshot with its catalog and data, file by file` and S13.1's other refractiveindex.info facts keep their assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the adapter lands, a test MUST instantiate the real `MaterialSourceProxy.createPtbOcdb` over a fixture snapshot under the test output, its fetch MUST parse a record through `PtbOcdbText` with its uncertainties under the file's hash, the stamp's version, CC-BY-4.0 and PTB's citation, and its update MUST run the snapshot body it shares with refractiveindex.info; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a PTB OCDB source without a snapshot answers no version and refuses search and fetch`, `a PTB OCDB snapshot lists its data records, and a fetched record is the reader's material with CC BY 4.0 and its citation`, `a PTB OCDB update keeps the data records and the licence file of the repository archive`, `a PTB OCDB archive without its licence file is refused and the held snapshot kept` and the unchanged `an update downloads the archive and replaces the snapshot with its catalog and data, file by file`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s44 invariants MUST pass.
